menu "Michi OTA"

config MICHI_OTA_MANIFEST_MAX_BYTES
    int "Maximum signed manifest size in bytes"
    default 2048
    range 1024 2048
    help
        Upper bound for the signed update manifest JSON downloaded from the
        manifest URL. The buffer lives on the HEAP (not the task stack);
        this bound is capped at 2048 so the heap spend stays small and the
        relation to the OTA task stack (MICHI_OTA_STACK_BYTES) stays
        predictable: the stack only carries mbedTLS + HTTP frames.
        Manifests larger than the bound are rejected at fetch time (the
        JSON content may be up to one byte less than this bound, which
        reserves the NUL terminator).

config MICHI_OTA_URL_MAX
    int "Maximum manifest URL length in characters"
    default 256
    range 64 1024
    help
        Upper bound for the manifest URL accepted by michi_ota_start() and
        for the binary URL inside the manifest. Longer URLs are rejected
        with ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG.

config MICHI_OTA_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "HTTP timeout for manifest fetch and firmware download (ms)"
    default 10000
    range 1000 60000
    help
        Per-read timeout for the esp_http_client during the manifest fetch
        and the firmware download. The download aborts cleanly on read
        failure (esp_ota_abort); there are no read retries.

config MICHI_OTA_STACK_BYTES
    int "OTA task stack size in bytes"
    default 10240
    range 4096 16384
    help
        Stack for the OTA task: it runs the whole update pipeline
        (manifest fetch, mbedTLS verification, streaming download,
        runtime SHA-256). The large transfer buffers (manifest up to
        MICHI_OTA_MANIFEST_MAX_BYTES, 4 KB download chunk) are
        heap-allocated, so the stack only has to carry mbedTLS + HTTP
        frames; 10240 leaves headroom for those frames.

endmenu
